# Commit messages

Format: `type: short imperative summary`, lowercase after the colon, no
trailing period.

Types: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `chore`, `docs`, `test`.

```
feat: add role-based route guard
fix: prevent duplicate refresh-token insert on concurrent requests
refactor: extract auth into shared auth-client lib
```

- One commit per logical change — don't bundle an unrelated fix into a
  feature commit.
- An optional body (bullet list) explains *why*, not a line-by-line diff recap.
- Write it like a human engineer would; don't mention AI tooling in the message.
